      {
        "id": 237301,
        "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-05-06T14:30:23.253Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Near mint after the first game couldn’t quite get enough uses out of Oblivaeon Shard + Mecha-Knight before Voss came out in phase 3, but it was close. Second game went better, ending it before Voss showed up at all.</p>\n<p>Being Oblivaeon, I can’t really give specifics, but replacing Dr. Medico with base Tempest, then letting him go down allows the “All heroes are immune to Infernal” trick to avoid the worst of Oblivaeon’s damage. If you switch everyone to zone 2 first turn, you will flip the shield on his next turn. Also, Form the Mecha-Knight doesn’t work so well with Dark Mind out, so keep that in mind.</p>\n<p>Legacy is always good with Heroic Interception/Take Down, and Benchmark, Chrono-Ranger, and Stuntman are good to give the Oblivaeon shard as they do lots of damage instances. I don’t like H=3 Oblivaeon as it doesn’t really give enough turns between the Scions and Oblivaeon, but it does make it easier to do combos like Shard+Knight.</p>\n<p>Also, interaction I didn’t know before, discarding for Omni-Unity, but putting the card under the Missile Pods, makes the mission not flip.</p>\n<p>~A-Kat</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-05-06T14:31:38.499Z",
